# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and let each platform check out what it
# uses natively. Git was already doing this via core.autocrlf on the maintainers' machines;
# stating it here makes it a property of the repo rather than of each developer's global
# git config.
#
# Working-tree line endings are deliberately NOT enforced by ESLint. With LF stored in the
# repo, a Windows checkout has CRLF and a Linux checkout has LF, so a linebreak-style rule
# can only ever pass on one platform -- the previous 'windows' setting made npm run lint
# fail on every Linux checkout, CI included.
* text=auto
